    <bpmn:process id="W_W290" name="W290. Hierarchical Category Structure Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Introduction of new product lines or reorganization of existing merchandising departments
Frequency: Quarterly/Semi-Annually
Volume: ~1–2 tree reorganizations per year; minor node additions monthly
Owner: Master Data Manager
Participants: VP Merchandising, Category Manager, BI/Data Analyst, Master Data Analyst
Source: workflow W290 — Hierarchical Category Structure Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W290_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W290_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W290_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W290_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W290_Lane2" name="BI">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W290_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W290_Lane3" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W290_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W290_Lane4" name="Master Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W290_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W290_Lane5" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W290_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W290_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W290_Start7" name="Introduction of new product lines or reorganization of existing merchandising departments">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W290_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W290_Task8" name="Hierarchy Proposal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Hierarchy Proposal: Merchandising proposes a change to the category tree (e.g., splitting &quot;Tools&quot; into &quot;Hand Tools&quot; and &quot;Power Tools&quot;).
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W290_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W290_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W290_Task9" name="Impact Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Impact Assessment: BI Analyst assesses reporting impact and legacy mapping. Master Data Manager assesses reclassification effort for existing SKUs.
Responsible (R): BI/Data Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W290_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W290_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W290_Task10" name="Approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Approval: VP Merchandising approves the new multi-level category structure (MDM-007).
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W290_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W290_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W290_Task11" name="System Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System Execution: Master Data Analyst creates the new nodes (Department, Category, Sub-Category, Class), and executes a batch reclassification script for affected SKUs.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Master Data Manager
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W290_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W290_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W290_Task12" name="Downstream Sync">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Downstream Sync: The new hierarchy is synced to the Data Warehouse (for BI reporting) and Ecommerce (for website navigation).
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W290_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W290_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W290_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W290_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W290_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-328 (ensure controlled execution — Foundational Masters (PA-29.1).) | - operational: Master Data Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Master Data Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W290_Assoc15" sourceRef="W290_Annotation14" targetRef="W290_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W290_Flow16" sourceRef="W290_Start7" targetRef="W290_Task8" />
