    <bpmn:process id="W_W309" name="W309. Bank &amp; Banking Partner Master Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New bank account opening, new banking partner relationship, bank branch closure/merger, store opening requiring deposit account linkage, or e-wallet/digital payment partner onboarding
Frequency: ~5–10 bank account additions/year (new store openings); ~2–3 banking partner changes/year; ~10–15 store deposit account linkages/year at the 10–15 new stores/year canon
Volume: ~210–230 bank accounts across 5 entities and 4 banking partners (BDO, BPI, Metrobank, Chinabank — operating/payroll/escrow/LC/float), incl. ~200 store deposit accounts; ~200 store deposit points; ~5 e-wallet settlement accounts
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: Finance Controller, AP Supervisor, Payroll Manager, IT ERP Administrator, Master Data Analyst
Source: workflow W309 — Bank &amp; Banking Partner Master Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W309_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W309_Lane1" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W309_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W309_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W309_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W309_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W309_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W309_Lane2" name="Master Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W309_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W309_Lane3" name="IT ERP Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W309_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W309_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W309_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W309_Start5" name="New bank account opening, new banking partner relationship, bank branch closure/merger…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W309_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W309_Task6" name="Bank Master Record Creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Bank Master Record Creation: Treasury Manager requests creation of a new bank master record when a new banking relationship is established. Request specifies: bank name, SWIFT/BIC code, Philippine bank code (BRSTN — Bank Routing Symbol Transit Number), clearing code (PhilPaSS), and branch details. Master Data Analyst creates the bank master in the ERP.
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W309_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W309_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W309_Task7" name="Entity Bank Account Setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Entity Bank Account Setup: Treasury Manager requests creation of a new bank account in the ERP. Request specifies: entity (one of 5), bank, branch, account number, account type (operating, payroll, escrow, LC, float, deposit), currency (PHP/USD), GL account mapping (bank clearing account, bank sub-ledger), authorized signatories, and online banking access details. Finance Controller approves the GL mapping. IT ERP Administrator configures the bank account and links it to the relevant ERP modules (AP payment, payroll disbursement, treasury cash position, AR collection).
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / IT ERP Administrator
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W309_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W309_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W309_Task8" name="Store Deposit Account Linkage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Store Deposit Account Linkage: For each of the 200 stores, Master Data Analyst links the store location (W254) to its designated bank deposit point. Configuration specifies: store code, nearest bank branch, deposit account number, deposit type (cash, check, e-wallet settlement), and CIT armored car deposit schedule (W174). This linkage drives the automatic store-level cash reconciliation in W5F and the bank deposit auto-matching in W30.4.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 10 min/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W309_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W309_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W309_Task9" name="E-Wallet &amp; Digital Payment Partner Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: E-Wallet &amp; Digital Payment Partner Configuration: For e-wallet settlement (GCash, Maya, GrabPay, ShopeePay — FIN-032), IT ERP Administrator configures: partner name, settlement account, settlement frequency (T+1, T+2), MDR rate per partner, reconciliation mapping (settlement file → POS transaction matching), and chargeback dispute workflow linkage.
Responsible (R): IT ERP Administrator
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 30 min/partner</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W309_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W309_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W309_Task10" name="Payment File Format Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Payment File Format Configuration: IT ERP Administrator configures the bank-specific payment file formats for AP disbursements (BDO, BPI, Metrobank, Chinabank — each uses different file layouts). Formats include: payroll bank credit file (HR-012), AP vendor payment file (W7), LC payment instruction (W232), and intercompany settlement file (W14). Treasury Manager validates the format by running a test payment file before go-live.
Responsible (R): IT ERP Administrator / Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 1 hour/bank</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W309_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W309_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W309_Task11" name="Bank Detail Change Governance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Bank Detail Change Governance: When a bank account needs to be modified (e.g., account closure, branch merger, signatory change), Treasury Manager initiates a change request. For entity-level bank accounts: Finance Controller approves. For vendor bank detail changes: the existing 48-hour cooling-off period (W287 Step 5) applies. All changes are logged in an immutable audit trail with old value, new value, approver, and effective date.
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W309_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W309_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W309_Task12" name="Periodic Bank Master Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Periodic Bank Master Review: Annually, Treasury Manager reviews all bank master records: (a) verifies account status with actual bank statements, (b) confirms authorized signatories are current, (c) validates that e-wallet MDR rates match current contracts, (d) confirms payment file formats are compatible with any bank system updates, (e) deactivates closed/unused accounts.
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W309_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W309_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W309_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W309_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W309_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-328 (ensure controlled execution — Foundational Masters (PA-29.1).) | - operational: upgrade, causing bulk payment file rejection and delayed vendor payments
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W309_Assoc15" sourceRef="W309_Annotation14" targetRef="W309_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W309_Flow16" sourceRef="W309_Start5" targetRef="W309_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W309_Flow17" sourceRef="W309_Task6" targetRef="W309_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W309_Flow18" sourceRef="W309_Task7" targetRef="W309_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W309_Flow19" sourceRef="W309_Task8" targetRef="W309_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W309_Flow20" sourceRef="W309_Task9" targetRef="W309_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W309_Flow21" sourceRef="W309_Task10" targetRef="W309_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W309_Flow22" sourceRef="W309_Task11" targetRef="W309_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W309_Flow23" sourceRef="W309_Task12" targetRef="W309_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W309_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W309_plane" bpmnElement="W_W309">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W309_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W309_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W309_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W309_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W309_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W309_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W309_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W309_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Task11_di" bpmnElement="W309_Task11"><dc:Bounds x="1450" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Task12_di" bpmnElement="W309_Task12"><dc:Bounds x="1660" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_Start5_di" bpmnElement="W309_Start5"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W309_End13_di" bpmnElement="W309_End13"><dc:Bounds x="1890" y="487" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
