    <bpmn:process id="W_W400" name="W400. Equipment &amp; Asset Maintenance (EAM) Master Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Procurement of new store fixtures, material handling equipment (MHE), or HVAC systems requiring maintenance tracking
Frequency: Monthly (as new equipment types are acquired)
Volume: ~5,000 trackable equipment records; ~200 maintenance plans
Owner: Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate / Maintenance Manager
Participants: Maintenance Manager, Master Data Analyst, Procurement Manager
Source: workflow W400 — Equipment &amp; Asset Maintenance (EAM) Master Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W400_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W400_Lane1" name="Master Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W400_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W400_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W400_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W400_Lane2" name="Maintenance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W400_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W400_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W400_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W400_Start4" name="Procurement of new store fixtures, material handling equipment (MHE), or HVAC systems…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W400_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W400_Task5" name="Equipment Template Creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Equipment Template Creation: Procurement Manager provides specs for a new equipment model. Master Data Analyst creates the Equipment Master template, defining the manufacturer, model, warranty duration, and serial number tracking requirement.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W400_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W400_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W400_Task6" name="BOM Definition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: BOM Definition: Maintenance Manager defines the equipment Bill of Materials (BOM), mapping standard spare parts (linked to Item Master W252) needed for repairs.
Responsible (R): Maintenance Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W400_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W400_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W400_Task7" name="Maintenance Plan Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Maintenance Plan Configuration: Maintenance Manager establishes standard preventative maintenance (PM) schedules (e.g., 6-month HVAC servicing, 200-hour forklift check).
Responsible (R): Maintenance Manager
Accountable (A): Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate
Duration: 20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W400_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W400_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W400_Task8" name="System Setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System Setup: Master Data Analyst configures the PM schedules and ties them to the Equipment Master in the ERP/EAM module.
Responsible (R): Master Data Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W400_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W400_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W400_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W400_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W400_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-328 (ensure controlled execution — Foundational Masters (PA-29.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Director, Facilities &amp; Real Estate / Maintenance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
